Story Image Agent is a multimodal AI workflow that converts storybook images into structured story knowledge and high-quality image-generation prompts.

The system uses Groq's Qwen Vision model for image understanding, LangGraph for agent orchestration, and LangSmith for evaluation. 
Generated prompts are automatically validated using:
semantic similarity, 
hallucination detection, 
story coverage checks, 
token tracking, and 
latency analysis before being approved and stored.

Key Features:

• Multimodal story understanding
• Character, setting and moral extraction
• AI image prompt generation
• Automated quality evaluation
• Hallucination detection
• LangSmith observability and evaluation
• LangGraph workflow orchestration

